 "result_text": "`create_pull_request` in `git_machete/github.py` now sends the POST to GitHub straight away. It no longer calls `derive_pull_requests` first to look for an existing PR. I didn't run any tests, and flake8 isn't installed here, so the edit is unlinted.\n\nIf a PR for that branch already exists, GitHub answers with a 422. The existing 422 handling then turns that into an `UnprocessableEntityHTTPError` carrying GitHub's message. The old error text, which gave the existing PR's link and details, is gone. What the user sees now is whatever GitHub's response body says.\n\nI also removed the `find_or_none` import, which nothing else in that file used.",
